<title>TUNISIA: Libyan plane lands in Saudi with haj pilgrims.</title>
<headline>Libyan plane lands in Saudi with haj pilgrims.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1997-03-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>A Libyan Arab Airlines plane carrying pilgrims for the annual Moslem haj landed in Jeddah in Saudi Arabia, the official Libyan news agency JANA reported on Saturday.</p>
<p>The agency, monitored in Tunis, did not say when the aircraft landed.</p>
<p>Libya is under U.N. Security Council sanctions, including an air embargo, for failing to hand over to Britain or the United States two Libyan suspects in the 1988 Lockerbie bombing of a Pan Am arliner over Scotland.</p>
</text>
